uctal carcinoma <italic>in situ</italic> in Australia in 1995</article-title><source>ANZ J Surg</source><year>2002</year><volume>72</volume><fpage>708</fpage><lpage>715</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'ANZ J Surg||72|708||bib16|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12534380</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Silverstein</surname><given-names>MJ.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The University of Southern California&#x0002f;Van Nuys prognostic index for suctal carcinoma <italic>in situ</italic> of the breast</article-title><source>Am J Surg</source><year>2003</year><volume>186</volume><fpage>337</fpage><lpage>343</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Am J Surg||186|337||bib17|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14553846</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Solin</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Recht</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Fourquet</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kurtz</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuske</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>McNeese</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>McCormick</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Cross</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Schultz</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Bornstein</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name><name><surname>Spitalier</surname><given-names>J-M</given-names></name><name><surname>Vilcoq</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Fowble</surname><given-names>BL</given-names></name><name><surname>Harris</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Goodman</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ten-year results of breast-conserving surgery and definitive irradiation for intraductal carcinoma (ductal carcinoma <italic>in situ</italic>) of the breast</article-title><source>Cancer</source><year>1991</year><volume>68</volume><fpage>2337</fpage><lpage>2344</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer||68|2337||bib18|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1657351</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thomson</surname><given-names>JZ</given-names></name><name><surname>Evans</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Pinder</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Burrell</surname><given-names>HC</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>ARM</given-names></name><name><surname>Ellis</surname><given-names>IO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Growth pattern of ductal carcinoma <italic>in situ</italic> (DCIS): a retrospective analysis based on mammographic findings</article-title><source>Br J Cancer</source><year>2001</year><volume>85</volume><fpage>225</fpage><lpage>227</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Br J Cancer||85|225||bib19|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11461081</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>W&#x000e4;rnberg</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Bergh</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Holmberg</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prognosis in women with a carcinoma <italic>in situ</italic> of the breast: a population-based study in Sweden</article-title><source>Cancer Epidemiol Biomarkers Prev</source><year>1999</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>769</fpage><lpage>774</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer Epidemiol Biomarkers Prev||8|769||bib20|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10498395</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zheng</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Holford</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name><name><surname>Flannery</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Boyle</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Time trend of female breast carcinoma <italic>in situ</italic> by race and histology in Connecticut, USA</article-title><source>Eur J Cancer</source><year>1997</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>96</fpage><lpage>100</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Eur J Cancer||33|96||bib21|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9071907</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>